TEST 38476 -- ATMF - crosslink
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-21, tb470
DUT:    IE520 4-member VCStack, AMF node "IE520-stk"
Peer:   AR4050S-5G, AMF node "4050-5g" (AMF master at this point)
AMF:    network-name "tb470"; po1 (LACP aggregate) converted from
        "switchport atmf-link" to "switchport atmf-crosslink" on BOTH ends.

VERDICT: PASS

STEP -- "Check DUT can join an AMF network when it is using a crosslink"

  Applied on both ends:  interface po1 / no switchport atmf-link
                                       / switchport atmf-crosslink

  Link type changed, read on the master:
    Local  Link       Link    ATMF    Adjacent    Adjacent Link
    Port   Type       Status  State   Node/Area   Ifindex  State
    po1    Crosslink  Up      Full    IE520-stk   4751     Forwarding

  DUT still joined:  Network Name tb470 / Role Member / Current ATMF Nodes 2

  PASS -- the DUT joined and stayed joined with the link configured as an ATMF
  crosslink.

POSITIVE EVIDENCE THAT THE SEMANTICS REALLY CHANGED (not just a label):

  Under "switchport atmf-link" (T38473):
      IE520-stk  parent domain = 4050-5g    node depth = 1
  Under "switchport atmf-crosslink" (this case):
      IE520-stk  parent domain = none       node depth = 0
      4050-5g    parent domain = none       node depth = 0
  i.e. the two nodes became PEERS in one domain rather than parent/child.
  That is the defining behaviour of a crosslink, and it is the reason this is
  graded PASS rather than "the link came up".

  Crosslink detail read on the master:
    Port                     : po1          Port Status  : Up
    Port State               : Full         Last event   : AdjNodeLSEPresent
    Adjacent Node Name       : IE520-stk
    Adjacent MAC             : 0000.cd37.0d6f      <-- the stack VIRTUAL MAC,
                                confirming the whole 4-member stack is the
                                adjacent node, not one member
    Crosslink Ports Blocking : False
    Node.Ifindex             : 4050-5g.4751 - IE520-stk.4751
    Link State               : Full - Full

CAVEAT -- with only two AMF nodes on this bench this is a degenerate crosslink.
Crosslinks exist to join multiple nodes at the same level of a domain; a
two-node crosslink exercises the mechanism but not the topology it is for.

